<title>FRANCE: EU leaves wheat, flour taxes unchanged - officials.</title>
<headline>EU leaves wheat, flour taxes unchanged - officials.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday left taxes applying to daily wheat grain and flour exports and other daily measures unchanged, member country officials said.  </p>
<p>The daily or &quot;common right&quot; export channel currently has a &quot;nil value&quot; entry on all non-taxed export business excluding rye flour which has a standing refund of 30 Ecus per tonne.</p>
<p>&quot;Nil value,&quot; also known as a &quot;dash,&quot; means export licences are valid for a shorter than normal period of 30 days, cannot be prefixed in advance and leave exporters vulnerable to a tax if one is imposed before the day they are used. It equally means exporters would pick up a refund if one were introduced before the licences are used.</p>
<p>Current wheat export taxes are as follows (Ecus per tonne) -- soft wheat grain 5.00, soft wheat flour 7.00, durum wheat grain 10.00 and durum groats 15.00.</p>
</text>
